WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.909 --> 00:00:13.953
The third graders were restless.

2
00:00:14.473 --> 00:00:18.395
They wanted to be playing outdoors, not sitting in the classroom.

3
00:00:19.495 --> 00:00:21.636
Mr. Higgins stood in front of the class.

4
00:00:21.656 --> 00:00:23.677
"What happens in spring?"

5
00:00:24.077 --> 00:00:24.677
he asked.

6
00:00:24.697 --> 00:00:27.919
"We plan for summer vacation!"

7
00:00:28.439 --> 00:00:29.119
said Katie.

8
00:00:29.139 --> 00:00:32.148
"True," said Mr.

9
00:00:32.188 --> 00:00:34.990
Higgins. "But it's not time for that yet, Katie.

10
00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:36.650
Who has another answer?"

11
00:00:37.911 --> 00:00:39.051
"Flowers bloom!"

12
00:00:39.611 --> 00:00:40.272
said Laura.

13
00:00:40.292 --> 00:00:42.653
"Birds build nests!"

14
00:00:43.253 --> 00:00:43.973
said Joy.

15
00:00:43.993 --> 00:00:46.795
"Good," said Mr.

16
00:00:46.815 --> 00:00:48.815
Higgins. "What about the weather?"

17
00:00:48.835 --> 00:00:55.298
"Sunny and warm," Katie said, looking out the window with longing.

18
00:00:55.318 --> 00:00:59.560
"But sometimes it can be stormy," said Luke.

19
00:01:00.984 --> 00:01:03.966
"Twisters!" said Carlos Ramirez.

20
00:01:04.487 --> 00:01:06.648
He lived two houses down from Luke.

21
00:01:06.668 --> 00:01:09.590
"That's right," said Mr.

22
00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:13.973
Higgins. "Twisters, or tornadoes, often strike in the spring.

23
00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:16.535
Who can explain what a tornado is?"

24
00:01:18.217 --> 00:01:19.618
Carlos spoke up again.

25
00:01:19.638 --> 00:01:22.860
"It's a strong wind that spins around and around.

26
00:01:24.261 --> 00:01:28.324
It's shaped like a funnel, and it hangs down from a storm cloud.

27
00:01:29.352 --> 00:01:32.154
A tornado can carry off a cow or a school bus.

28
00:01:32.714 --> 00:01:34.575
It can even lift a house up in the air!"

29
00:01:34.595 --> 00:01:39.898
"Tornadoes are very dangerous," agreed Mr.

30
00:01:39.938 --> 00:01:43.701
Higgins. "That's why every spring we prepare.

31
00:01:44.161 --> 00:01:46.742
We practice what to do if a tornado comes."

32
00:01:46.763 --> 00:01:50.125
"Are we going to have a tornado drill?"

33
00:01:50.525 --> 00:01:51.705
Katie asked hopefully.

34
00:01:51.725 --> 00:01:53.627
"Yes, Katie.

35
00:01:53.887 --> 00:01:55.248
Later," said Mr.

36
00:01:55.288 --> 00:01:59.166
Higgins. "Now who remembers what the tornado alarm sounds like?"

37
00:01:59.186 --> 00:02:02.589
"Three siren blasts!"

38
00:02:03.369 --> 00:02:03.950
said Luke.

39
00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:06.972
"Yes," said Mr.

40
00:02:06.992 --> 00:02:11.415
Higgins. "Then we all get in line, and I lead the way to the basement."

41
00:02:12.596 --> 00:02:14.958
"And when we get there, we take cover!"

42
00:02:15.478 --> 00:02:16.159
said Katie.

43
00:02:16.179 --> 00:02:18.841
"HA! That's the best part!"

44
00:02:20.482 --> 00:02:22.483
"Thank you, Katie," said Mr.

45
00:02:22.523 --> 00:02:26.662
Higgins. "Now who wants to demonstrate the take-cover position?"

46
00:02:26.682 --> 00:02:28.523
"I do!"

47
00:02:29.063 --> 00:02:29.824
cried Katie.

48
00:02:29.844 --> 00:02:33.566
"Please settle down, Katie," said Mr.

49
00:02:33.606 --> 00:02:35.027
Higgins, frowning a little.

50
00:02:35.047 --> 00:02:37.688
"Carlos, why don't you show us?"

51
00:02:39.169 --> 00:02:41.130
Carlos walked to the front of the class.

52
00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:45.452
He knelt on the floor and put his arms and hands over his head.

53
00:02:45.472 --> 00:02:48.294
"Perfect!" said Mr.

54
00:02:48.314 --> 00:02:51.436
Higgins. The third graders cheered.

55
00:02:51.956 --> 00:02:54.357
Carlos grinned and returned to his desk.

56
00:02:55.757 --> 00:02:57.097
"We're ready for the drill!"

57
00:02:57.578 --> 00:02:58.178
said Mr.

58
00:02:58.198 --> 00:03:00.798
Higgins. "Now get out your math homework."

59
00:03:02.019 --> 00:03:03.319
Everybody groaned.

60
00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:07.860
After math came social studies and then lunch.

61
00:03:08.361 --> 00:03:12.122
When the children returned from the lunchroom, it was time for art.

62
00:03:12.142 --> 00:03:16.963
"Let's work on our tornado posters," announced Mr.

63
00:03:16.983 --> 00:03:20.324
Higgins. "Katie, please pass out the magic markers."

64
00:03:21.556 --> 00:03:29.638
Katie grabbed the coffee can filled with markers when suddenly— weeee-uuuuu, weeee-uuuuu, weeee-uuuuu.

65
00:03:29.678 --> 00:03:32.439
Katie jumped and the markers flew into the air.

66
00:03:32.459 --> 00:03:35.500
"Tornado drill!"

67
00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:36.780
shouted Luke.

68
00:03:37.921 --> 00:03:40.382
The speaker on the wall crackled and hissed.

69
00:03:41.562 --> 00:03:42.122
Then Ms.

70
00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:43.863
Olson's voice filled the room.

71
00:03:43.883 --> 00:03:47.524
"Students!" the principal reminded them.

72
00:03:47.544 --> 00:03:51.176
"Go immediately to the basement."

73
00:03:51.196 --> 00:03:53.658
Everyone moved toward the door except Katie.

74
00:03:54.238 --> 00:03:55.679
She was picking up markers.

75
00:03:55.699 --> 00:03:59.162
"Get in line, Katie," Joy said.

76
00:03:59.182 --> 00:04:02.604
"I am," Katie snapped back.

77
00:04:03.125 --> 00:04:05.566
She hated it when Joy told her what to do.

78
00:04:07.348 --> 00:04:09.049
The third graders followed Mr.

79
00:04:09.089 --> 00:04:12.091
Higgins. They went down the stairs to the basement.

80
00:04:13.272 --> 00:04:16.214
Other students entered the basement from all directions.

81
00:04:16.234 --> 00:04:19.136
"Everybody down!"

82
00:04:19.572 --> 00:04:23.074
Mr. Higgins called as soon as everyone was standing by the wall.

83
00:04:24.235 --> 00:04:27.677
All the children dropped to the floor in the take-cover position.

84
00:04:28.798 --> 00:04:31.860
Ms. Olson held up her stopwatch and gave it a click.

85
00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:34.621
"Two minutes exactly," she said.

86
00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:36.162
"Good work, everyone!"

87
00:04:37.904 --> 00:04:39.625
Back in the classroom, Mr.

88
00:04:39.665 --> 00:04:42.066
Higgins passed out a paper to each student.

89
00:04:42.086 --> 00:04:44.808
"We'll finish our posters later.

90
00:04:46.032 --> 00:04:50.696
This is a list of things you can do at home to get ready for tornado season," he

91
00:04:50.776 --> 00:04:55.640
said. "You should each organize a Family Tornado Safety Team."

92
00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:58.583
"Cool," said Luke.

93
00:04:58.603 --> 00:05:02.606
"The Ramirez Tornado Safety Team!"

94
00:05:03.106 --> 00:05:03.967
said Carlos.

95
00:05:03.987 --> 00:05:07.730
"The Donovan Tornado Safety Team!"

96
00:05:08.331 --> 00:05:09.051
said Katie.

97
00:05:10.172 --> 00:05:14.236
She scribbled something on a piece of notebook paper and then passed it to Joy.

98
00:05:15.429 --> 00:05:16.391
Joy frowned.

99
00:05:16.932 --> 00:05:21.403
She could already guess what her sister's note said: I'll be captain!
